A||||4||Stoic||Anyone ever experience this?||||5||
Z||000000||Stoic||04-03-2001||05:20 PM||||I'm not sure if this will make any sense, but here goes.  I have a 4 cyl./auto.  I was on the highway last night doing about 100 kms/hr.  and the rpms began to slip up (about 3-400).  I pulled over and checked the tranny fluid (first instinct).  Plenty there.  It wouldn't slip when it was around 80kms/hr or under, so I drove it home nursing it.  I took it into work today and discovered that the slip is gone.  Instead, once I get upto speed, it is constantly reving at the point it was slipping to (if that makes sense).  So, I have less power, and it's loud (no exhaust leaks).  The rpms like I said only sit 3-400 higher, but it sounds like a lot more than that.  It also tends to stall periodically when idling in gear (connection?).  I was told the computer can cause this (I don't know if thats's true), or maybe it is the transmission (hopefully not).  Any ideas would be greatly appreciated.  I tend to trust opinions here more than taking it to a mechanic and letting them "$troubleshoot$".<BR>If any of this is unclear, let me know and I'll try to explain better.  <BR>(Sorry for the lengh) <P>------------------<BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||5
Z||000001||DRH||04-03-2001||05:40 PM||||Sure sounds like a Torque Converter Lockup problem. It is most likely the electric solenoid inside the transmission that has gone bad. This solenoid IS controlled by the computer (ECM) so that could be the problem also, but the solenoid is more likely and is a fairly common problem with this type of transmission. I've never done it myself, but have heard it can be replace by someone with moderate mechanical ability.<P>the ogre has an article about what the TCC is and what it does. Check the 'Ogre's Cave' link at the bottom of any page on the Forum.I've seen step by step instructions somewhere on replacing it but I can't remember where or find it in my links. Maybe someone else can help.<p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 04-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Stoic||04-03-2001||05:57 PM||||Thanks DRH, that helps a lot.<P>------------------<BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||6
Z||000003||Oreif||04-03-2001||06:08 PM||||That is exactly what it is, The TCC solenoid is going bad. I had a shop change mine when they installed the shift kit. But from what I understand it isn't too complicated to change. Just slightly messy. (Trans fluid)||||reg||1
